Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_release_keeps_every_count_exact`.

The defect: a release gives the object back to its own region and stops. It reads as the mirror of
a carve from a leaf, but every ancestor keeps counting an object that has left its kernel table,
and the root's subtree reaches its ceiling on objects that are gone.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(counts.exact, "a count drifted from the subtree")`, on a
release from the child or the grandchild.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/table.rs
